## Inventory Draw

One draw on one `StockLot`: what a roast, a sale or a count takes, at the lot's cost. Fields: `sku`, `lot`, `asset` (the inventory account the lot sits in), `qty` (thousandths of a unit), `costMinor`, and the cost split `part5000Minor` (green coffee and roasting) and `part5100Minor` (packaging), which must add up to `costMinor`.

RoastBatch carries its inputs as `containsMany(Draw)`; Fulfillment and CountAdjustment carry `draws`. Each document's `postings()` credits the draw's `asset` account for `costMinor`, and its `post` operation checks every split. The matching `StockLot.draw` operation, sent in the same batch, checks the cost against the lot's remaining rate and reduces the lot.

```ts
import { Draw } from '@cardstack/catalog/cards/accounting/ledger-stock';

@field draws = containsMany(Draw);
```

### Non-goals
Does not choose the lot or compute its own cost; whoever enters the document picks lots oldest first.
